    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9fdfeff1_c4a3299a",
        "filename": "doc/source/contributor/services.rst",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 339,
      "author": {
        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T16:39:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah - I agree, but I\u0027ve come up short with ideas on how to do that.\n\nIf people follow the template we use in keystone, they\u0027ll be writing integration tests since the APIs are called with a token. We have the luxury of using tokens in protection tests without requiring another service.\n\nWe talked about this a little bit with Patrole in Denver, but we never really came to a conclusion on how we can re-use things sanely.\n\nI\u0027m hoping that people are more familiar with the tests now that we\u0027re merging more of the patches (not only in keystone, but in other services, too). Maybe it\u0027s time to revisit this and see if we can find a better solution for re-use than developer documentation in oslo.policy.",
      "parentUuid": "9fdfeff1_7756c95e",
      "revId": "cc44258f8a67c4fe8c0e8c2a710a9ec7c01f255e",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9fdfeff1_7777a9d5",
        "filename": "doc/source/contributor/services.rst",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 364,
      "author": {
        "id": 8482
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-28T16:23:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "or an API that only requires read-level access - and it would be good to mention somewhere in here how admin implies member implies reader so that people understand it\u0027s okay to have a policy use the reader role",
      "revId": "cc44258f8a67c4fe8c0e8c2a710a9ec7c01f255e",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
